A||||11||artherd||Perfect Night!!!||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||10-05-2001||06:44 AM||||My Friend John (Mr2 guy) and I were driving (he randomly decided he wanted <BR>to go to his post office box in ... wherever... <P>Anyway, he's driving.  He wanted to drive the car, so I <BR>let him for a while in a closed area, and he did *really* <BR>well actually, so I got to enjoy being a Fiero Passanger <BR>for a while.  The T-tops are so great, you can look right <BR>up at the moon and the stars and the clouds and it's enough <BR>to just make you blury-eyed at times.<P>Eventually we pulled the tops entirely and turned on the <BR>heater as it was about 11pm Friday night on the coast.<P>So we're driving back through San Francisco, and we're <BR>in a left-hand turn lane on a 4-lane road waiting for <BR>the light to change...  when a black as midnight Lotus <BR>Esprit comes tearing out from the left!!  <BR>FOLLOW THAT CAR I command!   <BR>Light still red, we make a quick, questionably legal right <BR>turn onto the 6-lane Embarcadaro thingie.   We're right <BR>behind him already, so we just cruse with him ('cruseing <BR>in a Turbo Lotous.... **V8!!** It is a new V8 Twin Turbo <BR>Esprit with Beverley Hills dealer tags still affixed <BR>(Yes, we were close enough to read them... anyway, <BR>cruseing in a V8 Lotus is an attention-commanding pace as is... :)<P>We're side-by side, doing about 50, and about now he notices us, <BR>we give a friendly wave, and he waves back, and grins!   We cat <BR>and mouse, just playing, enjoying mutual mid-engine-coolness.<P>We come to the inevetable (and obligatory in any car story) red light.<BR>There's a cute bubbly looking burnette girl in the passanger seat, <BR>and she gives the *International Symbol for 'Rock-on'!!!* with both hands!<P>The light changes, and he... chrups and *takes off!*  John botched the <BR>start pretty badly actually (he later tells me he was busy and lost checking <BR>the girl out, he is too easially and too throughly distracted ;)<P>The Lotous is now ~20feet infront of us, and still pulling first gear, as are we.  <BR>He lifts briefly and *SHOOTS FIRE* out his georgous-sounding aftermarket exhaust <BR>system, the flat 180degree crank V8 barks and backfires once more, then he's *on* <BR>it again into second, *really* taking off now, he's ~35feet infront of us.  <P>Being the gentle and honourable sportsman that he is, he backs off, and we <BR>enjoy another half mile of cat-and-mouse and mutual stares of admiration <BR>at each other's vehicle!  All four of us were just grinning like madmen, <BR>having a great time just basking in each other's glory.<P>It was, is, and will remain a beautiful moment, but it came time for us <BR>to part when the roads split, ours into a (traffic lighted) left turn <BR>lane, his into a "stop-on-red-right-turn-is-only-a-suggestion" right turn.<P>He waved, I blew the girl a kiss, and he turned right, and *mashed* it!!  My <BR>god this guy had a Lotus and *knew how to drive it!*  He got sideways at <BR>about 55-60 (this is a 90degree corner, 2 lanes), and modulated just enough <BR>to control the slide and use it to *scream* off into the distance, leaving <BR>fond happy memories.<P>Driving away, we mutually realised that, as both of us came out of the <BR>run-for-fun with mid-engine sports cars, we really all won that night ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
